{
  "about": "The pair link in the helper's window (rust-helper protocol-and-mirror.md, \"The pair link\"): every app parses these, builds the same text back from the fields, and refuses each link under \"refused\" for the reason given. The payload rides in the URL fragment, which a browser never sends; key_hex is the 32-byte pairing key, base64url without padding in the link. mdns (the computer's own .local host name) and hid_hex (the helper install's 16-byte id, base64url without padding in the link) come after name when present; a case without them is a link that carries neither (an older helper's), and each is read on its own.",
